							</category>
							<category name="S&SForeverV8">
								<category name="Description">
									<comment>By Aaron0000</comment>
									<comment>S&S FOREVER 8.0</comment>
									<comment>Completely overhauls the Scav manufacturer into S&S from Borderlands 1.</comment>
									<comment>List of Changes;</comment>
									<comment>Most Scav items (excluding class mods/oz kits and some unique/legendary items) have been reskinned and renamed. Names and prefixes are based off of space objects and the like. Only "Scav" thing that remains is the logo in the item cards.</comment>
									<comment>S&S Weapons have been globally rebalanced. The stats should be fairly balanced in all aspects (minus a penalty in fire rate). S&S weapons also have a 25% increased chance to inflict a status effect compared to other non-Maliwan manufacturers.</comment>
									<comment>Several Uniques Weapons and Legendary Weapons have been replaced or adjusted. Details down below.</comment>
									<comment>If using the community patch, load this file after the community patch. In general, load this file last.</comment>
									<comment>Main Feature;</comment>
									<comment>Main feature of S&S weapons is their "limitless" magazine. Weapons cost nothing to fire at all. However, holding a weapon drains ammo from your ammo pool instead.</comment>
									<comment>DUE TO PRE-SEQUEL LACKING ANY FORM OF ROCKET LAUNCHER AMMO REGENERATION, ROCKET LAUNCHERS SIMPLY BEHAVE NORMALLY IN THIS VERSION.</comment>
									<comment>Ammo drain scales with level. At level 1, weapons should be draining fairly slowly, while at level 70 they should be roughly draining at the fire rate of the weapon (give or take).</comment>
									<comment>Weapons that cost more than one ammo per shot drain more ammo accordingly.</comment>
									<comment>Magazine and Reload accessories would be largely redundant with the magazine effect. Magazine accessories now reduce the draining of ammo by 20%, and reload effects increase Elemental Status Effect chance and damage.</comment>
									<comment>Other notes;</comment>
									<comment>If using the community patch, load this file after the community patch. In general, load this file last.</comment>
								</category>
								<category name="Extended Description">
									<category name="Gun Replacer List">
										<comment>Replacers</comment>
										<comment>Zim 		 -> 	Tarandus</comment>
										<comment>Badaboom 		 -> 	Cassiopeia</comment>
										<comment>Meat Grinder 	 -> 	Thanatos</comment>
										<comment>Boss Nova		 -> 	Draco</comment>
										<comment>Party Popper	 ->	Orion</comment>
										<comment>Boganella		 ->	Crux</comment>
									</category>
									<category name="Gun Descriptions">
										<category name="Tarandus">
											<comment>100% elemental chance under most circumstances.</comment>
											<comment>Significantly increased elemental damage.</comment>
											<comment>Increase in fire rate.</comment>
											<comment>Slight damage penalty.</comment>
										</category>
										<category name="Cassiopeia">
											<comment>Fires five rockets in the shape of the constellation Cassiopeia.</comment>
										</category>
										<category name="Orion">
											<comment>Fires one round that divides into three upon impact with a surface.</comment>
											<comment>Spawns in Shock only (but will not delete incendiary versions).</comment>
											<comment>Increased Accuracy.</comment>
											<comment>Increased elemental chance.</comment>
										</category>
										<category name="Draco">
											<comment>Dual-element weapon with large splash radius. Incendiary and Explosive.</comment>
											<comment>Boosted damage and fire rate.</comment>
											<comment>Fires in the shape of the constellation Draco.</comment>
										</category>
										<category name="Thanatos">
											<comment>Increased melee damage.</comment>
											<comment>Increased movement speed.</comment>
											<comment>Reduces Action Skill Cooldown time when held.</comment>
										</category>
										<category name="Crux">
											<comment>Increased daamge.</comment>
											<comment>Damage dealt is always explosive, regardless of weapon card information.</comment>
											<comment>Highly accurate.</comment>
											<comment>Spread is in the shape of a cross.</comment>
											<comment>Reduced ammo drain rate.</comment>
										</category>
									</category>
								</category>
								<category name="Prefixes">
									<category name="Shared Prefixes">
										<code profiles="">set GD_Weap_Shared_Names.Name.Prefix_Bandit.Prefix_Grip_Bandit PartName Eternal</code>
										<code profiles="">set GD_Weap_Shared_Names.Name.Prefix_Bandit.Prefix_Grip_Jakobs PartName Supernal</code>
